1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,000
Most diaries have one author.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:05,160
This one sometimes has two.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,580
This is Ghost Diary.

4
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:11,980
I start with an ordinary page: a

5
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,780
yellow umbrella, a chipped blue cup, and

6
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,020
the quiet rituals before bed.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,260
On the next page, the hook is

8
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:26,100
empty.

9
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:28,380
I save my words, then pass the

10
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,220
night.

11
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:32,460
Gemma runs locally, reading this entry and

12
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:33,980
a little of its history.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,880
It leaves a sentence I never wrote,

14
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,600
and remembers the umbrella's bent spoke.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,600
I traced the bent spoke with my finger.

16
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,560
My original is untouched.

17
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,040
I can see exactly what changed, compare

18
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,680
both versions, and restore my own words

19
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,040
with a single click.

20
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:10,160
The diary stays in my browser.

21
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,840
Gemma writes locally through Ollama.

22
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,120
Windows speech gives the added sentence a

23
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,360
voice, right on this device.

24
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,760
A private notebook.

25
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,760
An uninvited author.

26
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,280
Ghost Diary.

27
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:29,240
Your words, until they're not.
